<title>FRANCE: French Feb industrial production up 1.6 pct.</title>
<headline>French Feb industrial production up 1.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE said on Thursday industrial production, excluding construction, rose 1.6 percent in February from the previous month and was up 1.6 percent year-on-year. Industrial production excluding energy, agri-food businesses and construction -- considered by INSEE the best measure of manufacturing output -- rose 3.7 percent in Februray from the previous month, giving a year-on-year rise of 2.2 percent.</p>
<p>It gave the following seasonally adjusted data based on a new index introduced in January 1996.  </p>
<p>						    Feb 97 Jan 97  Nov 96</p>
<p>Industrial production index (base 1990)*100.9   99.3  100.4</p>
<p>Manufacturing output*			  98.4   94.9   96.0</p>
<p>  Agri-food				     111.2  108.7  111.9</p>
<p>  Energy					  108.7  120.0  191.1</p>
<p>  Semi-finished goods			 103.1   98.4  100.3</p>
<p>  Industrial capital goods		   87.3   85.4   85.9</p>
<p>  Car Industry				  105.8  100.7  101.3</p>
<p>  Consumer goods				 99.5   97.8   98.1</p>
<p>  Construction				   90.1   79.8   88.7</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted percentage changes:</p>
<p>					Feb vs Jan  Jan vs Dec   yr/yr</p>
<p> Industrial production index	1.6	 -1.1	   1.6</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		 3.7	 -1.1	   2.2</p>
<p> Agri-food				2.3	 -2.9	   1.4</p>
<p> Consumer goods			 1.7	 -0.3	   0.9</p>
<p> Car industry			   5.1	 -0.6	   0.1</p>
<p> Industrial capital goods	   2.2	 -0.6	   1.3</p>
<p> Semi-finished goods		  4.8	 -1.9	   3.6</p>
<p> Energy				  -9.4	  0.8	  -1.8</p>
<p> Construction			  12.9	-10.0	  -2.7</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom + 33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
</text>
